From: Batman <noreply@batman.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bluez: remove advertising instances before powering off (#254 D3c)

winson3QQ/Batman#254 P2 (docs/design/254-p2-impl.md §22). Adds bluez feed patch 901 (src/adapter.c,
src/advertising.c/.h): adapter_shutdown() queues Remove Advertising (all) on the adapter's mgmt ahead of
SET_POWERED off. A power-off keeps advertising instances without a timeout and the next power on enables
them again before batman-provd checks its preconditions (04 wsl.20 btmon, 2026-11-01). Made on the tree
with 900 applied (both edit src/adapter.c).

Batman-Witness: file usr/bin/bluetoothd Batman: advertising instances removed before power off
--- /dev/null
+++ b/feeds/packages/utils/bluez/patches/901-batman-adv-remove-before-poweroff.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+Batman #254 D3c: remove advertising instances before powering off (docs/design/254-p2-impl.md §22)
+
+adapter_shutdown() powered the adapter off without removing the advertising instances; the kernel
+keeps instances without a timeout across a power-off and enables them again at the next power on,
+before the advertiser (batman-provd) checks its preconditions. Queue Remove Advertising (all) on the
+adapter's mgmt ahead of SET_POWERED off, while the controller is still powered.
+
+--- a/src/adapter.c
++++ b/src/adapter.c
+@@ -10929,6 +10929,11 @@
+ 
+ 		clear_discoverable(adapter);
+ 		remove_temporary_devices(adapter);
++		if (adapter->adv_manager) {
++			btd_adv_manager_remove_all(adapter->adv_manager);
++			info("Batman: advertising instances removed before power off (hci%u)",
++							adapter->dev_id);
++		}
+ 		set_mode(adapter, MGMT_OP_SET_POWERED, 0x00);
+ 
+ 		adapter_remaining++;
+--- a/src/advertising.c
++++ b/src/advertising.c
+@@ -2027,3 +2027,17 @@
+ 
+ 	queue_foreach(manager->clients, manager_refresh, NULL);
+ }
++
++/* Batman #254 D3c: remove every advertising instance of this adapter. Queued
++ * on the adapter's mgmt (FIFO, one request at a time) by adapter_shutdown()
++ * ahead of SET_POWERED off, so the removal runs while the controller is still
++ * powered: a power-off keeps instances without a timeout and the next power on
++ * would advertise them again, outside the advertiser's control.
++ */
++void btd_adv_manager_remove_all(struct btd_adv_manager *manager)
++{
++	if (!manager)
++		return;
++
++	remove_advertising(manager, 0);
++}
+--- a/src/advertising.h
++++ b/src/advertising.h
+@@ -15,3 +15,4 @@
+ 							struct mgmt *mgmt);
+ void btd_adv_manager_destroy(struct btd_adv_manager *manager);
+ void btd_adv_manager_refresh(struct btd_adv_manager *manager);
++void btd_adv_manager_remove_all(struct btd_adv_manager *manager);
